WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>An unknown frontier</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>On the map painted by my heart</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>When I open the door, the path goes on</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>I'm kicking up dust as I</i>
<i>start running to your town</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Along a route where earth and sky meet</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Riding the rushing southern wind</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Slicing through the wind</i>
<i>dyed blue by the sky</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>I'm rushing out with my whole heart</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Shooting past the midday moon</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Towards a world different</i>
<i>from what we've known before</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>I will keep on running through to the end</i>

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>However far</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:22.559
Since the breakdown of ceasefire negotiations
yesterday it's a melee here in Taboli City,

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.062
with the army of the Republic of Balic,
anti-government guerrillas,

00:02:25.062 --> 00:02:29.691
and a number of armed militias from various
factions all engaged in fierce armed conflict.

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:32.653
Numerous assaults and acts of
cruelty have been witnessed,

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:35.197
causing the atmosphere inside
the city to be extremely tense.

00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:38.575
Also, in a medical facility
just outside the city,

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:40.035
about 100 refugees...

00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:41.662
have been stranded...

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.657
Al. Test the data links.

00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:19.658
Roger.

00:03:19.658 --> 00:03:22.369
ADM, on. PCL, contact.

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:25.330
Opening from 403 to 412.
Commencing TAC transfer.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.916
"The Ending Day By Day"
Commencing TAC transfer... Complete.

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:29.126
"The Ending Day By Day"
Check the secondaries too.

00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:30.127
Roger.

00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:31.795
Bad news from the observation team.

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:33.672
It looks like we're
running late for the party.

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:36.967
That's just fine by me.
The hero always arrives late.

00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:37.968
Idiot!

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.012
I'm not going to help you
if something goes wrong for you.

00:03:40.012 --> 00:03:41.722
Oh man, that's cold.

00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:42.931
Colonel Maress,

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:46.727
the only people here are sick or elderly,
or else women and children.

00:03:46.727 --> 00:03:50.981
If you have even a little human
compassion, please let us go.

00:03:50.981 --> 00:03:53.066
Gebo 4 to all units.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.735
We've arrived at Point Echo.

00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:57.070
Activating ECS.
Now in stealth mode.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.364
Opening cargo bay hatches.

00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:01.116
I... I'm begging you.

00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:03.994
If you do something like this,
God will never forgive...

00:04:05.746 --> 00:04:07.039
Uruz 2, roger.

00:04:07.039 --> 00:04:08.707
You all heard that, right?
Are you ready?

00:04:08.707 --> 00:04:13.712
I don't give a damn. Least of all
about the god<i> your </i>lot believe in.

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:15.088
Colonel Maress...

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.257
This is Uruz 6.
I'm<i> okay </i>to go!

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.387
This is Uruz 7.
Ready to drop.

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:23.889
Die!

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.819
What the...

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:45.827
This is Uruz 6.
I'm in firing position.

00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:47.788
Let's get this party started!

00:04:53.752 --> 00:04:55.170
Defend the perimeter!

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.840
Red 1 is... Red 1 is...

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.716
Dammit! Radio and sensors are down!

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:01.760
What's going on?
Are they jamming us?

00:05:03.178 --> 00:05:05.389
AS spotted!
Gunner, fire at will!

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:08.684
Calm down!

00:05:08.684 --> 00:05:11.103
Close formation!
There aren't very many of them.

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:34.001
Colonel Maress, who in the
world are those guys?

00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:36.003
They couldn't possibly be
the anti-government forces...

00:05:36.003 --> 00:05:37.171
They're Mithril.

00:05:37.171 --> 00:05:38.422
Mithril?

00:05:38.422 --> 00:05:39.923
I've heard of them before.

00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:42.885
I've heard rumors that
there's an elusive mercenary

00:05:42.885 --> 00:05:45.888
force not aligned with any government.

00:05:45.888 --> 00:05:48.515
They have weaponry ten years in
advance of the rest of the world

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:50.726
and extraordinary personnel.

00:05:50.726 --> 00:05:51.768
Apparently they interfere
in international conflicts,

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:53.770
acting like they're some sort of peacekeepers.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.981
But I never thought<i> I'd </i>ever see them...

00:05:55.981 --> 00:05:58.901
But why would people like
them help the refugees?

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.777
I have no idea.

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:02.863
But you saw those AS units, didn't you?

00:06:02.863 --> 00:06:05.866
Not even the Americans have
that kind of machinery yet.

00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:08.785
It has to be them.
Mithril has come!

00:06:08.785 --> 00:06:10.787
I suggest we call in reinforcements, Colonel.

00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:13.874
Absolutely. Throw everything we've got at them.

00:06:13.874 --> 00:06:15.876
Don't let those mercenaries
leave here alive.

00:06:15.876 --> 00:06:17.669
Or those heretic refugees, either!

00:06:19.421 --> 00:06:21.298
Mike 13 destroyed.

00:06:21.298 --> 00:06:23.884
All hostile targets neutralized.

00:06:23.884 --> 00:06:25.344
Master mode 6.

00:06:25.344 --> 00:06:27.346
Stay on alert with active sensors.

00:06:27.346 --> 00:06:29.056
Roger.

00:06:29.056 --> 00:06:31.391
Uruz 2 to Uruz 6, Uruz 7.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.393
Defend the perimeter around the camp.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.854
Secure a landing area for the choppers.

00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:36.980
Uruz 7, roger.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.565
Uruz 6, roger.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.902
This is Gebo 4.

00:06:41.902 --> 00:06:43.904
I'm descending on the landing area.

00:06:43.904 --> 00:06:45.906
You'd better do a good job protecting my ass.

00:06:45.906 --> 00:06:48.534
Heh! Sorry, I don't go for guys' asses.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:51.453
Just hurry and load up.

00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:52.871
Whatever.

00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:04.091
We'll take the wounded on first!

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:05.843
All men, help out!

00:07:05.843 --> 00:07:07.261
Women and children,

00:07:07.261 --> 00:07:09.930
gather in one place and stay where you
are until you receive further notice!

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:13.934
But man, they're nothing but
old men, old ladies, and kids.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:17.271
Why did the enemy bother to attack them?

00:07:17.271 --> 00:07:20.107
That's what ethnic conflicts are like.

00:07:20.107 --> 00:07:21.608
Well, but in this case,

00:07:21.608 --> 00:07:24.278
there are probably some
more complicated issues.

00:07:24.278 --> 00:07:26.280
Politics?

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.990
Economics too.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.951
They probably use actions that go
against international peace treaties

00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:33.871
to give the major countries a
suitable amount of provocation,

00:07:33.871 --> 00:07:36.290
and then look at the results
to decide who to approach

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:40.085
for backroom deals in the rights to
their mineral resources or whatever.

00:07:40.085 --> 00:07:43.380
Our involvement is a part of all that, too.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.133
Absolutely disgusting, isn't it?

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.385
But it was worth coming here.

00:07:48.385 --> 00:07:50.262
Exactly.

00:07:50.262 --> 00:07:52.848
Tiwaz 12, what's your situation?

00:07:52.848 --> 00:07:54.641
This is Tiwaz 12.

00:07:54.641 --> 00:07:57.644
There are two combined-arms companies
approaching from the northwest.

00:07:57.644 --> 00:08:00.731
Near coordinates 36A, 87A.

00:08:00.731 --> 00:08:04.401
12 AS units, 12 MBTs, and a lot more.

00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:06.278
Looks like you've still got time
before they reach you, but...

00:08:07.446 --> 00:08:09.031
Crap!

00:08:12.034 --> 00:08:13.118
It's Triple A!

00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:15.621
I've taken a hit fired from the
hill 10 km southwest of here.

00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:17.164
The engine and pressure gauge are damaged.

00:08:17.164 --> 00:08:19.541
Unable to restart.
I'm going in for a crash landing.

00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:24.004
Tiwaz 12, are you okay?

00:08:24.004 --> 00:08:26.256
Tiwaz 12, respond!

00:08:26.256 --> 00:08:28.008
I'm still alive, somehow...

00:08:28.008 --> 00:08:30.177
I'll send you the data on
the Triple A immediately.

00:08:30.177 --> 00:08:32.679
We'll destroy this unit and run over your way.

00:08:35.182 --> 00:08:37.142
An anti-ECS missile?

00:08:37.142 --> 00:08:40.020
Nobody ever told me these guys
had such advanced equipment.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.982
Yeah, this is bad. Our choppers
are going to get shot down.

00:08:43.982 --> 00:08:46.276
Uruz 2, we can't take off now.

00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:48.028
As soon as we reach 150 feet,

00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:49.488
a missile will take us down
and the refugees along with us!

00:08:49.488 --> 00:08:52.699
I know. But enemy troops are coming.

00:08:52.699 --> 00:08:55.702
How good are you at NOE flight?
We'll give you an escort.

00:08:55.702 --> 00:08:58.038
Follow along alternate route two, and...

00:08:59.998 --> 00:09:01.375
Where are you going, Sousuke?

00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:03.168
I'll take down the anti-air missiles.

00:09:03.168 --> 00:09:04.419
What about the rendezvous?

00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:05.420
Find a way to handle it.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.421
We'll argue about it later.

00:09:07.422 --> 00:09:09.675
Understood.

00:09:09.675 --> 00:09:14.012
We'll guide the choppers
to coordinates 34B, 99A.

00:09:14.012 --> 00:09:15.055
Be careful.

00:09:15.055 --> 00:09:16.557
Roger.

00:09:16.557 --> 00:09:18.141
We don't have time to spare.

00:09:18.141 --> 00:09:21.645
If this keeps up, we'll all
be surrounded and killed.

00:09:21.645 --> 00:09:23.397
Report from the anti-air missile squad.

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:25.524
We've shot down an enemy chopper.

00:09:25.524 --> 00:09:29.194
Good. Keep holding them down.

00:09:29.194 --> 00:09:31.196
If we keep them pinned down on land,

00:09:31.196 --> 00:09:34.032
we'll be able to crush them
with our main troops.

00:09:34.032 --> 00:09:36.493
Relay the coordinates to the artillery!

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.258
This is Uruz 7.

00:09:51.258 --> 00:09:53.051
I'm closing in fast on the
enemy's antiaircraft installation.

00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:54.303
Five more minutes.

00:09:54.303 --> 00:09:56.013
This is Uruz 2.

00:09:56.013 --> 00:09:59.057
Moving away from camp.
Distance from destination is...

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.268
That was close.

00:10:01.268 --> 00:10:03.145
That was just a greeting.

00:10:03.145 --> 00:10:06.315
If we don't hurry, the enemy's going to
rain down artillery fire on those choppers.

00:10:06.315 --> 00:10:09.151
Looks like it's just a matter of
time before we're surrounded, huh?

00:10:09.151 --> 00:10:12.196
Even something as powerful as our M9s
won't be able to handle two companies.

00:10:12.196 --> 00:10:15.324
--I know that. If we fight here...
--Enemy AS units spotted.

00:10:15.324 --> 00:10:19.077
Two units. Bearing 048. Distance 15.

00:10:19.077 --> 00:10:21.038
Damn! They really are here!

00:10:21.038 --> 00:10:24.166
All units, stop. We're being
targeted by enemy AS units.

00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:25.584
Uruz 6, watch 4:00.

00:10:25.584 --> 00:10:26.210
Our altitude is...

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.462
Don't go any higher.

00:10:28.462 --> 00:10:29.421
Missile warning.

00:10:29.421 --> 00:10:32.758
--Two RF missiles detected, locked on Gebo 4.
--Activate ECM!

00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:34.468
Put the blip enhancer on max!

00:10:34.468 --> 00:10:35.761
Roger.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.643
I'm taking enemy fire.
This is getting bad.

00:10:42.643 --> 00:10:43.519
How are things over there?

00:10:43.519 --> 00:10:46.146
Almost done. All that's left is...

00:10:46.146 --> 00:10:47.147
I see them!

00:10:56.323 --> 00:10:59.076
One anti-air installment neutralized.

00:10:59.076 --> 00:11:01.662
Escape through the hole in their anti-air net.

00:11:01.662 --> 00:11:03.121
All Gebo units, did you hear that?

00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:05.123
We're pulling out of the
battle area immediately.

00:11:05.123 --> 00:11:08.919
Roger. Uruz 2 and Uruz 6, hurry up
and dock for the transport choppers.

00:11:08.919 --> 00:11:10.212
What about rendezvousing with Uruz 7?

00:11:10.212 --> 00:11:11.505
Impossible in the current situation.

00:11:11.505 --> 00:11:12.881
Gebo 7 is too badly damaged.

00:11:12.881 --> 00:11:14.675
And there's not enough fuel or time left.

00:11:14.675 --> 00:11:17.219
Besides, this hole in the anti-air
net will last a few minutes, tops.

00:11:18.262 --> 00:11:20.514
Don't worry about me,
go ahead and pull out.

00:11:20.514 --> 00:11:22.266
I'll get out on foot.

00:11:22.266 --> 00:11:24.560
I'm currently heading to
the alternate escape route.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.727
You can handle it, right?

00:11:25.727 --> 00:11:26.770
Affirmative.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.064
I have homework I need to hand in tomorrow,

00:11:29.064 --> 00:11:30.274
so I can't die here.

00:11:32.234 --> 00:11:34.444
Okay. Let's meet at the Danaan.

00:11:34.444 --> 00:11:35.279
Roger.

00:11:35.279 --> 00:11:36.446
You heard that, right?

00:11:36.446 --> 00:11:38.156
All units, pull out!

00:11:38.156 --> 00:11:42.244
We always end up mooning them
and then running away.

00:11:42.244 --> 00:11:43.662
How uncool.

00:12:03.557 --> 00:12:05.684
Gold 2 to all units.

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:09.271
The enemy AS is heading south
down Revolution Street alone.

00:12:09.271 --> 00:12:11.732
Set up a blockade at Point 03-21.

00:12:11.732 --> 00:12:13.233
Blue 1, acknowledged.

00:12:13.233 --> 00:12:15.777
Blue 1 to all Blue Team units.

00:12:15.777 --> 00:12:17.404
Form two lines and await further orders.

00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:19.656
You have permission to fire at will.

00:12:19.656 --> 00:12:21.825
--Good, good. Don't let that white AS escape,
--Inputting designated coordinates.

00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:23.577
--under any circumstances!
--Commencing to open fire.

00:12:28.332 --> 00:12:29.958
Shot cannon ammunition remaining: 0.

00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:30.834
I know that!

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:33.545
Missile warning. Bearing 128.

00:12:38.217 --> 00:12:40.385
Warning. MBT.

00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:04.743
What just happened?

00:13:04.743 --> 00:13:07.204
Success. Due to the Lambda Driver...

00:13:07.204 --> 00:13:09.414
Save the talk for later.
Damage report.

00:13:09.414 --> 00:13:11.667
Class B damage to the right shoulder.

00:13:11.667 --> 00:13:13.669
Malfunction in the stabilizers.

00:13:13.669 --> 00:13:16.004
Critical errors in the targeting system.

00:13:16.004 --> 00:13:17.840
Uruz 7 to Uruz 2.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.385
Due to enemy presence,
I've abandoned the alternate escape route.

00:13:21.385 --> 00:13:24.304
I've only taken minor damage,
but I'm getting surrounded.

00:13:24.304 --> 00:13:26.390
I don't have much ammo left, either.

00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:29.768
Uruz 2, do you copy?

00:13:31.353 --> 00:13:32.729
This is Uruz 7. Please res-

00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:36.316
This is the Tuatha de Danaan.
Teletha Testerossa speaking.

00:13:36.316 --> 00:13:38.277
Uruz 7, do you read me?

00:13:38.277 --> 00:13:38.944
Captain...

00:13:38.944 --> 00:13:41.738
--I have the transport helicopters on standby over the sea,
--Load SUBLARS into MVLS 8, 10,

00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:43.740
--under a communications blackout.
--12, 14, and 16.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:47.202
--Please follow my directions to escape.
--Input coordinates. Commence setting altitude.

00:13:47.202 --> 00:13:48.370
Roger.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.289
However, I must apologize.

00:13:50.289 --> 00:13:52.040
There were more enemy troops
than I had expected.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.126
At this point I do not have an escape route.

00:13:54.126 --> 00:13:57.045
Oh? I don't think that's quite true...

00:13:57.045 --> 00:13:58.547
I've transmitted the data to you.

00:13:58.547 --> 00:14:01.216
Please move to the position marked.

00:14:01.216 --> 00:14:02.384
There?

00:14:02.384 --> 00:14:05.512
--But I would be going right into the enemy...
--It's okay, just hurry up!

00:14:05.512 --> 00:14:07.431
Roger. Over and out.

00:14:09.892 --> 00:14:13.854
Depth, 100. 8 knots.
We've reached the target location.

00:14:13.854 --> 00:14:14.897
Very well.

00:14:14.897 --> 00:14:19.484
Activate the EMFC in active mode.
Turn 180 degrees and stand by.

00:14:19.484 --> 00:14:20.694
Aye, ma'am.

00:14:20.694 --> 00:14:24.865
Activate the EMFC.
Steer to port. Set course to 127.

00:14:24.865 --> 00:14:26.950
EMFC activated, active mode.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.328
Steering to port.
Course set to 127.

00:14:29.328 --> 00:14:31.455
Please brace for impact.

00:14:31.455 --> 00:14:34.833
Mr. Mardukas, maximum speed on my signal.

00:14:34.833 --> 00:14:36.710
Aye, Captain.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:41.548
Enemy AS is heading from
Anton Street to Rutpo Bridge.

00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:43.300
He's like a trapped rat.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:47.471
It's payback time for
destroying my precious weapons.

00:14:47.471 --> 00:14:49.890
Uruz 7 to TDDHQ.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:52.392
ETA to designated location, 2 minutes.

00:14:57.356 --> 00:14:58.815
They're playing cat-and-mouse with me.

00:14:58.815 --> 00:15:03.362
Warning. 1 AS, 1 IFV, dead ahead. Distance 5.

00:15:09.368 --> 00:15:11.328
Chain gun ammunition remaining: 0.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.091
Designated location reached.

00:15:27.427 --> 00:15:30.556
This is the 3rd Combined Armored Company.

00:15:30.556 --> 00:15:32.766
Silver Team and Copper Team,

00:15:32.766 --> 00:15:35.394
Green Team and Yellow Team,

00:15:35.394 --> 00:15:37.187
formation complete!

00:15:37.187 --> 00:15:38.772
This is the 8th Combined Armored Company.

00:15:38.772 --> 00:15:40.566
Gold Team and Platinum Team,

00:15:40.566 --> 00:15:42.359
Blue Team and Purple Team,

00:15:42.359 --> 00:15:43.402
formation complete!

00:15:43.402 --> 00:15:45.445
Sniping team, in position.

00:15:45.445 --> 00:15:47.447
All troops are in position.

00:15:47.447 --> 00:15:48.615
Good!

00:15:48.615 --> 00:15:50.117
This is Uruz 7.

00:15:50.117 --> 00:15:51.743
There are large enemy
forces on both sides of me.

00:15:51.743 --> 00:15:52.828
No ammo left.

00:15:52.828 --> 00:15:54.079
Escape is impossible.

00:15:54.079 --> 00:15:56.832
Recommend abandoning this unit and
activating the self-destruct mechanism.

00:15:56.832 --> 00:15:57.791
Rejected.

00:15:57.791 --> 00:15:59.168
I won't be able to get my school credits then.

00:15:59.168 --> 00:16:04.173
Attention Arm Slave Operator.
Attention Arm Slave Operator.

00:16:04.173 --> 00:16:06.508
We have you completely surrounded.

00:16:06.508 --> 00:16:08.051
--Emergency blow!
--You have nowhere to escape!

00:16:08.051 --> 00:16:08.468
--Aye, ma'am. Emergency Blow.
--You have nowhere to escape!

00:16:08.468 --> 00:16:10.429
--Aye, ma'am. Emergency Blow.
--Open the hatch and surrender!

00:16:10.429 --> 00:16:13.849
Main Ballast Tank Blow. Uptrim 5 degrees.

00:16:13.849 --> 00:16:15.809
I'll give you to the count of ten!

00:16:15.809 --> 00:16:17.978
Ten! Nine!

00:16:17.978 --> 00:16:20.147
Eight! Seven!

00:16:20.147 --> 00:16:21.940
Six! Five!

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:23.984
Four! Three!

00:16:23.984 --> 00:16:26.445
Two! One!

00:16:26.445 --> 00:16:27.487
What?!

00:16:37.706 --> 00:16:39.666
The Arbalest has been recovered.

00:16:39.666 --> 00:16:43.212
Let's give them a little "reward"
on our way out. Launch all SUBLARS!

00:16:43.212 --> 00:16:46.048
Roger. Launch all SUBLARS!

00:16:46.048 --> 00:16:48.425
Launching all SUBLARS. Aye!

00:16:48.425 --> 00:16:50.511
Maintain battle speed. Crash dive!

00:16:50.511 --> 00:16:52.471
Aye, ma'am. Crash dive!

00:17:16.495 --> 00:17:20.082
An amphibious submarine?!

00:17:20.082 --> 00:17:21.708
How is that even possible?

00:17:21.708 --> 00:17:24.545
Who in the hell are those guys?

00:17:41.854 --> 00:17:44.147
"Ii kuni tsukurou."

00:17:48.068 --> 00:17:51.029
"Ii kuni tsukurou."

00:17:51.029 --> 00:17:53.866
--Muromachi shogunate...
--It's the Kamakura! The Kamakura!

00:17:56.076 --> 00:17:58.787
That's a junior high school question!

00:17:58.787 --> 00:18:01.582
How do you expect to pass
the class like that, Sousuke?

00:18:01.582 --> 00:18:03.625
I'm bad at Japanese history.

00:18:03.625 --> 00:18:05.919
Not to mention Classics
and Modern Literature, too.

00:18:05.919 --> 00:18:09.840
And stop doing your homework after a mission!

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.593
I mean come on, you do something
straight out of a slick Bond movie,

00:18:12.593 --> 00:18:14.678
and you just go right back to the boring
nitty-gritty of life? It's sad to see!

00:18:14.678 --> 00:18:16.513
No can do. I'd fail the class.

00:18:16.513 --> 00:18:18.182
Who cares?

00:18:18.182 --> 00:18:20.684
Homework is something you
can just slap together!

00:18:20.684 --> 00:18:22.227
Kurz.

00:18:22.227 --> 00:18:25.606
That's what you say, but you've
barely written any of your reports!

00:18:25.606 --> 00:18:27.274
Oh, you mean this week's, right?

00:18:27.274 --> 00:18:28.901
And last week's too.

00:18:28.901 --> 00:18:31.528
The logistics unit keeps bugging me about it.

00:18:31.528 --> 00:18:34.364
Try putting yourself in my shoes a little bit.

00:18:34.364 --> 00:18:38.660
Oh, yeah... It must be rough
for "Big Sis" Mao, too...

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:42.581
It's all your fault, you know!<i> Yours!</i>

00:18:42.581 --> 00:18:43.081
That tickles...

00:18:43.081 --> 00:18:45.292
"794 A.D.: Capital transferred to Heiankyo."

00:18:50.672 --> 00:18:52.966
We've just passed 15 degrees north latitude.

00:18:52.966 --> 00:18:56.637
No ships have been detected
following us within a 30 mile radius.

00:18:59.014 --> 00:19:01.558
Set alert level to Yellow 3.

00:19:01.558 --> 00:19:03.769
I will now hand command over
to the Executive Officer.

00:19:03.769 --> 00:19:04.895
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:04.895 --> 00:19:07.689
Setting alert level to Yellow 3.

00:19:07.689 --> 00:19:09.608
Taking over command.

00:19:27.918 --> 00:19:28.961
Mr. Sagara?

00:19:28.961 --> 00:19:30.712
Captain!

00:19:30.712 --> 00:19:32.965
Oh, no, please sit down.

00:19:32.965 --> 00:19:35.259
I only came to eat dinner.

00:19:35.259 --> 00:19:37.261
--But...
--Don't worry about it.

00:19:38.011 --> 00:19:39.304
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:41.849 --> 00:19:43.058
Homework?

00:19:43.058 --> 00:19:43.892
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:43.892 --> 00:19:45.727
Is it difficult?

00:19:45.727 --> 00:19:48.021
Yes, ma'am.
At least to me...

00:19:48.021 --> 00:19:50.023
Why don't I teach you?

00:19:50.023 --> 00:19:53.151
No! I could never ask you to do such a thing!

00:19:53.151 --> 00:19:54.695
Just kidding.

00:19:54.695 --> 00:19:57.698
I knew you would say something like that.

00:19:57.698 --> 00:20:00.284
But it does look very difficult.

00:20:00.284 --> 00:20:03.704
Not at all. It is part of my mission, after all.

00:20:03.704 --> 00:20:04.663
Mission...

00:20:04.663 --> 00:20:07.624
"Important!" "Memorize this or die!" "Court-Martial!!"

00:20:09.251 --> 00:20:11.086
Captain.

00:20:11.086 --> 00:20:13.422
Thank you very much
for what you did for me today.

00:20:13.422 --> 00:20:15.716
You saved my life.

00:20:15.716 --> 00:20:18.218
Not at all. It was part
of my mission, after all.

00:20:18.218 --> 00:20:21.221
<i>He's late</i>!

00:20:21.221 --> 00:20:25.017
What is that idiot thinking, being out of
reach for two days straight all of a sudden?!

00:20:25.017 --> 00:20:27.728
He's still got the notes I lent him!

00:20:27.728 --> 00:20:30.063
I couldn't do my homework!
What's going on here?!

00:20:30.063 --> 00:20:33.734
Calm down, Kana-<i>chan</i>.
I'm sure Sagara has his reasons.

00:20:33.734 --> 00:20:35.777
We should give him a warm welcome back.

00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:37.070
No way!

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:38.655
It's like this every single freakin' time!

00:20:38.655 --> 00:20:40.866
Oh, Sagara.

00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:43.952
Sousuke! Give me back my notes!

00:20:43.952 --> 00:20:45.120
What?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.456
Sorry, Chidori. I forgot to bring them.

00:20:47.456 --> 00:20:49.666
Forgot?<i> Again</i>?!

00:20:49.666 --> 00:20:52.461
Then let's go back and get them, right now!
They're in your apartment, right?

00:20:52.461 --> 00:20:54.004
--That's impossible.
--Why?

00:20:54.004 --> 00:20:56.507
Because I left them in a submarine
two thousand kilometers away...

00:20:56.507 --> 00:20:59.051
"Kaname Chidori"

00:20:59.593 --> 00:21:01.845
"Merida Island Conference Room"
This is the anti-air missile used by

00:21:01.845 --> 00:21:03.764
"Merida Island Conference Room"
government forces to shoot down Tiwaz 12.

00:21:04.181 --> 00:21:08.936
It is an improved version of the Patriot,
loaded with a powerful ECCS.

00:21:08.936 --> 00:21:11.104
This means that under the
appropriate conditions,

00:21:11.104 --> 00:21:13.357
our ECS will lose its
effectiveness against them.

00:21:13.357 --> 00:21:18.737
As of right now, only a limited number of
advanced countries have this kind of missile.

00:21:18.737 --> 00:21:21.615
But the Balic Government Army had them.

00:21:21.615 --> 00:21:25.118
How are we to interpret this,
Lieutenant Commander Kalinin?

00:21:25.118 --> 00:21:27.829
I can only assume that a
very powerful organization

00:21:27.829 --> 00:21:31.083
independently supplied
them with the missiles.

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:33.710
That's impressive technology and
a large amount of funds, then.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:34.670
Yes.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:38.006
What's more, there is a possibility
that they prepared this equipment

00:21:38.006 --> 00:21:40.884
in anticipation of our
intervention in this matter.

00:21:40.884 --> 00:21:42.386
So they have intelligence sources, too?

00:21:42.386 --> 00:21:43.345
Correct.

00:21:43.345 --> 00:21:46.807
And we can't be sure that this is unrelated
to the seajacking incident, either.

00:21:46.807 --> 00:21:52.688
Of course, I doubt the enemy is in a position
to freely detect all of our movements, but...

00:21:52.688 --> 00:21:53.897
They're dangerous.

00:21:53.897 --> 00:21:55.023
Indeed.

00:21:55.023 --> 00:21:58.861
We must be more cautious
in future operations.

00:21:58.861 --> 00:22:00.696
--Otherwise...
--I know.

00:22:03.156 --> 00:22:05.742
Otherwise, we will all die.

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.516
<i>I'm sure you're still looking</i>

00:22:29.516 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Straight ahead to tomorrow</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Just like you always have</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Just like the sunflowers</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>That bloomed on that windy hill</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>No matter how far apart we are</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>I pray that my singing will reach you</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>On nights when the tears never seem to stop</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.895
<i>I want to be the moon</i>

00:23:14.895 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>That shines through your window</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Because I believe we will meet again</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>No matter what</i>

00:23:45.175 --> 00:23:46.927
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.927 --> 00:23:49.847
<i>Daily life in Tokyo was no different than usual.</i>

00:23:49.847 --> 00:23:53.851
<i>But I didn't yet know that</i>
<i>in the shadows of that ephemeral peace,</i>

00:23:53.851 --> 00:23:56.270
<i>the wheels of a vast conspiracy</i>
<i>had started to move.</i>

00:23:56.270 --> 00:23:59.022
<i>Next time: "The Situation Beneath the Surface."</i>

00:23:59.022 --> 00:24:04.715
<i>Dangerous people gather,</i>
<i>drawn by the smell of gunpowder.</i>
